.TH SPOT 1 "2026-11-25" "spot 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
spot \- Spotlight-style launcher for GNOME
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B spot
.RB [ \-\-toggle | \-\-background | \-\-settings | \-\-quit ]
.br
.B spot \-\-search
.I query
.br
.B spot \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B spot
is a resident launcher.
Press
.B Super+Space
(handled by the
.I spot-helper@spot.dev
GNOME Shell extension), type, and press
.BR Enter .
It finds installed applications (desktop files) and AppImages, and also answers
calculations, system actions (lock, log out, suspend, restart, power off),
URLs, existing paths and web searches.
.PP
Without options,
.B spot
shows the launcher, starting the resident instance if needed.
Starting Spot from the application grid opens its settings window instead.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-toggle
Show the launcher, or hide it if it is shown.
Bind this to a custom shortcut if you don't use the GNOME Shell extension.
.TP
.B \-\-background
Start the resident instance without showing anything (used at login).
.TP
.B \-\-settings
Open the settings window: extension status, shortcut conflicts, start at login,
launch history.
.TP
.B \-\-quit
Stop the resident instance.
Needed after editing the configuration file.
.TP
.BI \-\-search " query"
Print the results for
.I query
and exit.
No display is needed.
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " \-V
Print the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/spot/config.ini
Optional settings: calculator, system actions, URLs and paths, web search and its URL.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/spot/history.tsv
Launch history used for ranking.
Delete it, or use the settings window, to forget it.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/spot/appimages/
Metadata and icons read from AppImages.
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/dev.spot.Spot.desktop
Present when \(lqStart at login\(rq is on.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SPOT_APPIMAGE_DIRS
Colon-separated folders to scan for AppImages instead of the defaults
(~/Applications, ~/AppImages, ~/.local/bin, Downloads, Desktop).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gnome-extensions (1)
